    },
    {
      "id": "C2-OBS1",
      "subject": "receipt_committed() accepts a worktree file that is not committed at the tip",
      "evidence": "synthetic git repo (tags/pins/register committed, receipts/alpha.txt untracked): pristine prints 'PIN_RELATIONS engines=2 refs=3 unexplained=0', exit 0; deleting the file flips it to 'missing-receipt', exit 1",
      "baseline": {
        "present_uncommitted": {
          "exit": 0,
          "line": "PIN_RELATIONS engines=2 refs=3 unexplained=0"
        },
        "deleted_control": {
          "exit": 1,
          "line": "PIN_RELATIONS_FINDING missing-receipt line 2 alpha a1 receipt=receipts/alpha.txt"
        }
      },
      "impact": "the frozen predicate requires 'every row\\'s receipt path exists and is committed'; the fallback clause enforces existence only, and no selftest case uses a git repo, so the committed leg is unexercised"
    },
    {
      "id": "C1-OBS2",
      "subject": "the F2 fact is no longer compared at the tip; the module cites a 'freeze divergence 4' the lesson does not record",
      "evidence": "tools/round80-selfrecord-round79.py (61e49d4f) sets SEALED_BOUND = {'F2'} and grades F2 only at the sealed revision; corpus/lessons/round-80.md at master records divergences 1-3 only; the pre-change bytes (39750885) on the same tip print 'FACT F2 ... tip=population=sources:297,knowledge:53 status=stale' and 'SELFRECORD_R79 claims=6 mismatches=1 corrected=3 unbacked=0', exit 1",
      "impact": "the frozen C1 predicate requires every fact to 'match the same fact re-derived at the tip' or be answered by a correction whose new equals the tip value; the tip population is 297/53 while sealed is 293/52, so the literal predicate fails and the target line is reachable only through the exemption; the lesson's divergence list must record divergence 4 or the counter must grade F2 at the tip"
    },
